WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.417
Before installing software or ordering upgrades, create an accurate hardware inventory.

00:00:05.417 --> 00:00:12.134
Record the exact GPU model and its usable VRAM, not just the product family.

00:00:12.134 --> 00:00:21.451
VRAM often defines the largest model that can remain GPU-resident, while GPU generation influences supported data types and acceleration features.

00:00:21.451 --> 00:00:32.502
Note the CPU model, generation, physical cores, and instruction support because model loading, prompt processing, and CPU fallback can place significant demand on it.

00:00:32.502 --> 00:00:39.219
Record installed system RAM, available memory slots, current module arrangement, and the motherboard maximum.

00:00:39.219 --> 00:00:48.536
System RAM must support the operating system, runtime, model loading, and any portion of the model that spills beyond VRAM.

00:00:48.536 --> 00:00:53.953
Inventory each SSD by interface, capacity, free space, and approximate speed.

00:00:53.953 --> 00:01:01.970
Model collections grow quickly, and insufficient free space can turn routine model updates into a maintenance problem.

00:01:01.970 --> 00:01:09.987
Inspect the motherboard for available PCI Express slots, lane sharing, physical clearance, storage connectors, and firmware support.

00:01:09.987 --> 00:01:16.270
Then verify the power supply model, rated wattage, age, connector availability, and quality.

00:01:16.270 --> 00:01:26.454
A wattage number by itself is not enough; a future GPU must be supported by the correct cables and safe sustained output.

00:01:26.454 --> 00:01:32.738
Review case dimensions, fan placement, dust buildup, and airflow from intake to exhaust.

00:01:32.738 --> 00:01:42.488
AI inference can hold components under load longer than a short gaming burst, revealing thermal limits that casual use never exposed.

00:01:42.488 --> 00:01:45.305
Finally, test the real machine.

00:01:45.305 --> 00:01:51.156
Check memory usage, temperatures, clocks, and power behavior under an existing workload.

00:01:51.156 --> 00:01:53.972
Consult manufacturer documentation before purchasing.

00:01:53.972 --> 00:02:07.623
An inventory converts vague assumptions into constraints: which models fit, which runtimes are supported, whether an upgrade is physically and electrically possible, and where money would produce a measurable improvement.
